===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[prevent]] [[harm]] or [[difficulty]].
## To [[help]] (somebody) to [[survive]], or [[rescue]] (somebody or something) from [[harm]].
##: {{ux|en|She was '''saved''' from drowning by a passer-by.}}
##: {{ux|en|We were able to '''save''' a few of our possessions from the house fire.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Billy Joel|authorlabel=no|title=w:You May Be Right|album={{w|Glass Houses (album)|Glass Houses}}|date=7 March 1980|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ilsv0C1-aBw|text=Turn out the light<br>Don't try to '''save''' me<br>You may be wrong for all I know<br>But you may be right}}
##* {{quote-journal|en|date=2014-06-14|volume=411|issue=8891| magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21604091-it-possible-sniff-out-problems-sewer-pipes-they-happen-its-gas It's a gas]| passage=One of the hidden glories of Victorian engineering is proper drains. Isolating a city’s effluent and shipping it away in underground sewers has probably '''saved''' more lives than any medical procedure except vaccination.}}
## To [[keep]] (something) [[safe]]; to [[safeguard]].
##* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=3|passage=Thou hast{{...}}quitted all to '''save''' / A world from utter loss.|year=1873}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=w:George Carlin| title=w:When Will Jesus Bring the Pork Chops?| url=https://archive.org/details/sacredmountainof0000john/| location=[[New York]]| publisher=w:Hyperion Books| ISBN=1-4013-0821-X| OCLC=757869006| OL=24604921M| page=132 |pageurl=https://archive.org/details/whenwilljesusbri00hype/page/132/| text=IF IT '''SAVES''' JUST ONE LIFE<br>You often hear a new policy or procedure justified by the specious idea that "If it '''saves''' the life of just one (insert here 'child' or 'American soldier'), it will be worth it." Well, maybe not. Maybe a closer look would show that the cost in time, money or inconvenience would be much too high to justify merely '''saving''' one life. What's wrong with looking at it like that? Governments and corporations make those calculations all the time.}}
## To [[spare]] (somebody) from effort, or from something undesirable.
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 8|act=2|scene=i|passage=I'll '''save''' you / That labour, sir. All's now done.}}
## {{lb|en|Christianity}} To [[redeem]] or [[protect]] someone from eternal [[damnation]].
##: {{ux|en|Jesus Christ came to '''save''' sinners.}}
## {{lb|en|sports}} To catch or deflect (a shot at goal).
##* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/0/football/19632463|title=Chelsea 6-0 Wolves
|passage=Chelsea's youngsters, who looked lively throughout, then combined for the second goal in the seventh minute. Romeu's shot was '''saved''' by Wolves goalkeeper {{w|Dorus De Vries}} but Piazon kept the ball alive and turned it back for an unmarked Bertrand to blast home.}}
## {{lb|en|baseball}} To preserve, as a [[relief pitcher]], (a [[win#Noun|win]] of another [[pitcher]]'s on one's team) by defending the lead held when the other pitcher left the game.
# To put aside; to avoid.
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[store]] for [[future]] [[use]].
##: {{cot|en|lay aside|lay away|lay by|lay in|lay up|put aside|put away|put by|store away|store up}}
##: {{ux|en|Let's '''save''' the packaging in case we need to send the product back.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[conserve]] or [[prevent]] the [[waste|wasting]] of.
##: {{ux|en|'''Save''' electricity by turning off the lights when you leave the room.}}
##* {{RQ:Christie Autobiography|I|4|passage=An indulgent playmate, Grannie would lay aside the long scratchy-looking letter she was writing (heavily crossed ‘to '''save''' notepaper’) and enter into the delightful pastime of ‘a chicken from Mr Whiteley's’.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en| date=May 21 2019|title=Facial recognition will soon be everywhere. Are we prepared?| journal=The Guardian| author=Dylan Curran| passage=However, we’ve reached the stage where our technological leaps and bounds no longer '''save''' us hours, or even minutes – they shave only seconds from our day-to-day tasks.
|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2019/may/21/facial-recognition-privacy-prepared-regulation}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[obviate]] or make [[unnecessary]].
##* {{RQ:Dryden Spanish Fryar
|passage=Will you not speak to '''save''' a lady's blush?}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive|computing|video games}} To [[write]] a [[file]] to [[disk]] or other [[storage medium]].
##: {{ux|en|Where did I '''save''' that document? I can't find it on the desktop.}}
## {{senseid|en|economize}} {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[economize]] or avoid waste.
## {{lb|en|transitive|and|intransitive}} To [[accumulate]] [[money]] or [[valuable]]s.
## {{lb|en|transitive|gambling|slang|archaic}} To make an [[agreement]] to give (some amount of [[money]]) to a [[fellow]] [[gambler]] if one [[win]]s, and to [[receive]] that amount from them if they win, as a form of [[hedge|hedging]].
##: {{ux|en|to '''save''' a fiver}}
## {{lb|en|reflexive|often|with|"for"}} To [[refrain]] from [[romantic]] or (''especially in later use'') [[sexual]] [[relationship]]s until one is [[married]] or is with a [[suitable]] [[partner]].
##: {{ux|en|She told me she's '''saving''' herself for marriage.}}
##* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}| genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]| location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts| year=2017|system=PC| scene=Tempest| oclc=1261299044| text=Ryder: Come on—you two were intimate, right?<br>Peebee: Take a wild guess. Why are people so hung up on sex? It's a natural expression of attraction.<br>Peebee: We were doing exciting, daring, irreverent things. It stirs stuff up. Like shaking up a bottle of champagne, you know?<br>Peebee: You ''should'' know, better than anyone...<br>Peebee: I'm not the type to "'''save''' myself".}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} To avoid [[say#Verb|saying]] something.
##: {{ux|en|'''Save''' your excuses and lies.}}
##* {{RQ:Noire Thug-A-Licious|page=206|passage=School days went by. I ran across Sly a couple a times, but I wasn't in no mood to talk. He could '''save''' all that philosophical bullshit he liked to holla. Didn't nobody need to tell me what was up.}}

====Usage notes====
* In computing sense “to write a file”, also used as phrasal verb {{m|en|save down}} informally. Compare other computing phrasal verbs such as {{m|en|print out}} and {{m|en|close out}}.

