# An instance of preventing (further) [[harm]] or [[difficulty]].
#* {{quote-av|en|author=Drachinifel|title=The Salvage of Pearl Harbor Pt 2 - Up She Rises!|date=18 November 2020|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DlLCe1WNaIE|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221022073855/https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DlLCe1WNaIE|archivedate=22 October 2022|accessdate=30 October 2022|time=0:34|text=As 1942 began, work was now continuing apace on getting the ships back afloat and into dock.  The first good news in this regard was ''West Virginia''.  Thanks to a combination of ''Tennessee''{{'}}s unintentional '''save''' and the crew's own efforts, she'd settled upright, and so divers estimated that, if the various holes could be patched and pumping done in a sensible order from the top down, she should just rise back up to the surface on an even keel, which, in turn, meant that a lot of the initial work on removing her main battery could now be stopped.}}
## In various [[sport]]s, a [[block]] that [[prevent]]s an [[opponent]] from [[scoring]].
##: {{ux|en|The goaltender made a great '''save'''.}}
##* {{quote-journal|en| date=December 29, 2010| author=Sam Sheringham| title=Liverpool 0 - 1 Wolverhampton| work=BBC| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9308904.stm| passage=Wolves defender {{w|Ronald Zubar}} was slightly closer with his shot on the turn as he forced {{w|Pepe Reina}}, on his 200th Premier League appearance, into a low '''save'''.}}
## {{lb|en|baseball}} A successful attempt by a [[relief pitcher]] to preserve the win of another pitcher on one's team.
##: {{ux|en|Jones retired seven to earn the '''save'''.}}
## {{lb|en|professional wrestling|slang}} A point in a professional wrestling match when one or more wrestlers run to the ring to aid a fellow wrestler who is being [[beat]]en.
##: {{ux|en|The giant wrestler continued to beat down his smaller opponent, until several wrestlers ran in for the '''save'''.}}
## {{lb|en|informal}} An action that brings one back out of an [[awkward]] [[situation]].
##: {{ux|en|Nice '''save'''.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} The act, process, or result of [[#Verb|saving]] [[data]] to a [[storage]] [[medium]].
#: {{ux|en|If you're hit by a power cut, you'll lose all of your changes since your last '''save'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The game console can store up to eight '''saves''' on a single cartridge.}}
# {{lb|en|RPG}} A [[saving throw]].

